1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,646
On Mars, the sunset is blue.

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,927
On Earth, it glows
red and orange.

3
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:09,854
Here, air scatters the blue
away, and the red gets through.

4
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:13,427
But Martian air is
full of very fine dust.

5
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:17,444
That dust lets blue light
through best, close to the Sun.

6
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:21,149
So around the setting
Sun, the sky turns blue.

7
00:00:21,783 --> 00:00:22,270
Uranus?

8
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:26,241
A NASA simulation shows
azure, fading to royal blue.

9
00:00:26,867 --> 00:00:28,934
And on the Moon,
no color at all.

10
00:00:28,934 --> 00:00:29,973
Just black.

11
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:32,719
Different world, different sunset.
